- Version: 0.2.9\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.24\par
- Summary: Renamed keepalive state labels to USB_TransportKeepAlive names, hid delay-plot data when no live client/keepalive exists, and hardened COM release around tool actions.\par
- Notes: `firmware/esp32c3_bridge/main/CommunicationFunctions.c` now reports keepalive runtime states as `USB_TransportKeepAlive_ServerSend` and `USB_TransportKeepAlive_ClientReturn` for clearer runtime visibility. `server/sim/link_state_machine.py` aligns display/log strings with the same naming. `server/ui/index.html` now suppresses and clears delay-plot samples when TCP/keepalive are both inactive, showing explicit N/A labels and a no-connection message instead of stale delay data. `scripts/idfw.cmd`, `scripts/idfw.ps1`, `scripts/flash_hidden.ps1`, and `scripts/monitor_capture.ps1` now release COM ports before and after actions to reduce stale lock failures.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-23 12:17:04\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.8\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.23\par
- Summary: Fixed simulator sine parameter responsiveness, added client keepalive live-status indicator, and synchronized simulator/client DataSimulation events.\par
- Notes: server/sim/data_payload.py now applies frequency to per-sample packet waveform generation so amplitude/frequency edits immediately change generated DATA payload values. server/ui/index.html adds Runtime Summary \"Client Live\" red/green indication mapped to keepalive states. server/sim/link_state_machine.py and firmware/esp32c3_bridge/main/CommunicationFunctions.c forward DataSimulationOn and DataSimulationOFF text events end-to-end so simulator and client toggles stay synchronized. README.md, AGENTS.md, and CLAUDE.md were updated with mandatory rule-gated build/flash sequencing.\par
