\b 2026-03-17 (estimated)\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.1\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.19\par
- Summary: First fully working version with end-to-end RESET -> INITIALIZE -> CONNECT -> KEEPALIVE cycle.\par
- Notes: Bridge INITIALIZE handler verified requiring data_ver=1 payload (BRIDGE_REALTIME_DATA_INTERFACE_VERSION=1). Bridge KEEPALIVE handler verified requiring rver=1 in client response. Bridge DATA frame confirmed: 170-byte binary payload. BRIDGE_FRAME_MAX_PAYLOAD = 256; client raised COMMUNICATION_FRAME_MAX_PAYLOAD to match. Transport fully operational: RESET -> INITIALIZE -> CONNECT -> KEEPALIVE cycle sustained continuously.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-17 (estimated)\b0\par
- Version: 0.2.0\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.19\par
- Summary: Major version bump for architecture change: server simulator refactored to new transport state machine and REST API surface.\par
- Notes: Introduced server/sim/link_state_machine.py as the active simulator runtime replacing controller_state.py. New LinkState enum, keepalive engine, port-alive detection, and force-release transport. Updated server/api/routes.py to new API surface. Added POST /api/transport/release-com endpoint. Version bumped to 0.2.0 reflecting the architectural change in transport ownership and state model.\par
