\b 2026-03-17 14:49:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.19\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.19\par
- Summary: Extracted ESP32-C3 communication runtime into dedicated CommunicationFunctions module and kept app_main as a thin entry wrapper.\par
- Notes: Added `firmware/esp32c3_bridge/main/CommunicationFunctions.c` and `CommunicationFunctions.h`, moved the long-running bridge transport loop into `communication_functions_run()`, kept `firmware/esp32c3_bridge/main/bridge_main.c` focused on `app_main()` delegation, and updated the firmware component CMake source list accordingly. Verified with successful `idfw.cmd build` and successful flash to `COM4`.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-17 14:52:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.18\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.18\par
- Summary: Split keepalive runtime states, moved last-delay -1 semantics to ESP32-C3 firmware telemetry, and expanded simulator UI diagnostics.\par
- Notes: `firmware/esp32c3_bridge/main/bridge_main.c` now reports controller-owned signed telemetry (`td_last_ms`, `td_max_ms`, `terr`) with `td_last_ms=-1` outside keepalive states and pushes telemetry updates on state transitions. `server/sim/link_state_machine.py` now parses signed delay telemetry and mirrors controller values directly. `server/ui/index.html` now includes synchronized pause controls across both loggers, telemetry reset actions, regex-based logger filtering, and a dedicated `SERVER/CLIENT DELAY` rolling plot with marker rendering and invalid-state highlighting. Architecture docs and README were aligned to `KeepAliveServerSend` and `KeepAliveClientReturn` naming.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-16 14:54:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.17\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.17\par
- Summary: Completed bridge-side keepalive protocol hardening and validated successful communication with the ESP32-S3 client.\par
- Notes: `firmware/esp32c3_bridge/main/bridge_main.c` now keeps keepalive request ownership fully server-side using `sid` plus `req` metadata, parses TCP frames immediately without wait-window RX blocking, retries the same pending request id on timeout, and avoids counter reseeding during retry attempts. The keepalive period was raised to 300ms to add timing margin while preserving the 0.3-second response deadline and three-attempt retry policy. Verified with successful build, successful flash to `COM4`, simulator launch on `127.0.0.1:8000`, and synchronized monitor sessions showing connect and keepalive progression with the updated protocol contract.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-13 19:50:00\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.16\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.16\par
- Summary: Shifted simulator-side transport behavior out of duplicate Python control paths and into the ESP32-C3 bridge while updating the UI and design docs.\par
- Notes: `firmware/esp32c3_bridge/main/bridge_main.c` now gates bridge keepalive traffic on the post-connect bridge state instead of raw socket accept, resets counters on connect entry, and continues owning the authoritative two-counter keepalive/watchdog flow. `server/sim/link_state_machine.py` now treats Python `connect` as a monitor-only state, removes duplicate USB `CONNECT` transmission during normal flow and retry flow, and keeps the host focused on reset/initialize, COM ownership, logs, and mirrored bridge state. The simulator UI/backend sources in `server/ui/index.html`, `server/api/routes.py`, and `server/transport/serial_link.py` carry the simplified control surface, COM-release handling, and transport cleanup changes, while the architecture diagrams and detailed design document were regenerated to match the current ownership split.\par
\par
\b 2026-03-12 14:34:13\b0\par
- Version: 0.1.15\par
- Firmware Version: 0.1.15\par
- Summary: Promoted the ESP32-C3 bridge from USB-only framing into the simulator SoftAP/TCP transport endpoint.\par
- Notes: `firmware/esp32c3_bridge/main/bridge_main.c` now brings up a visible `EyalSimulatorAP` SoftAP, owns a single-client TCP listener on `192.168.4.1:3333`, accepts framed transport traffic over both USB Serial/JTAG and TCP, and sends `client_connected` on TCP connect so the ESP32-S3 client can advance into keepalive. The bridge payload ceiling was increased to 256 bytes, stale TCP sessions are actively replaced or closed on reset, disconnect, and parse failure, and the transport design sources plus detailed design document were updated so the documented server-side flow matches the new firmware behavior.\par
- Resolved Defects:\par
  - BRIDGE-20260312-1: The ESP32-C3 bridge exposed only USB framing, so the ESP32-S3 client could not reach the simulator transport path over Wi-Fi/TCP.\par
\par
